         <notesStmt>
            <note type="project" target="dat1">This manuscript was probably produced in late 1890, shortly before Whitman offered the poems, unsuccessfully, to first <hi rend="italic">Arena</hi> and then <hi rend="italic">Scribner's</hi>.</note>
            <note type="work_relations" cert="high" target="xxx.00406 xxx.00564">These five groups of lines represent early stages of what eventually became two different short poems, "L. of G." and "L. of G.'s Purport," when first published in <hi rend="italic">Good-Bye My Fancy</hi> (1891). In late 1890, however, Whitman had attempted to publish poems containing these lines in other combinations and under different titles. (See editorial note for <ref target="loc.00231">loc.00231</ref>.)</note>
